      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Hamill Estate Agents are excited to present No. 6 Brian Boru Street, a charming two-bedroom mid-terrace tram cottage nestled in Clontarf one of Dublin’s most sought-after residential locations. Rich in character and history, this delightful home offers an exceptional opportunity for buyers seeking a property with original charm and the potential to create a truly bespoke residence.\r\n\r\nPositioned on the quiet and quaint Brian Boru Street, which runs parallel to Clontarf Road and the seafront, the property forms part of a unique terrace of historic single-storey cottages originally built to house Dublin's tram workers. Today, these distinctive homes remain highly regarded for their character, village-like atmosphere, and enviable coastal setting.\r\n\r\nStepping inside, the cottage immediately reveals a surprisingly spacious and welcoming interior. A generous living room is bathed in natural light thanks to its sunny southerly aspect, creating a warm and inviting space to relax and entertain. To the rear, a galley-style kitchen forms part of an extension incorporating the bathroom accommodation. The kitchen opens directly onto a private rear courtyard and garden, providing a peaceful outdoor retreat that is perfect for al fresco dining or simply enjoying the fresh coastal air.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation extends to approximately 42 sq.m (452 sq.ft.) and comprises two bedrooms, with one positioned to the front of the property and the second overlooking the rear garden. While presented in good condition throughout, the property offers an exciting opportunity for modernisation, allowing an incoming purchaser to enhance the existing layout and add their own style and personality.\r\n\r\nLocation is undoubtedly one of No. 6 Brian Boru Street's greatest assets. Just a short stroll from Clontarf Promenade, residents can enjoy scenic coastal walks stretching towards Bull Island and beyond. The vibrant cafés, restaurants, boutiques and shops of Vernon Avenue are all within easy walking distance, while nearby St Anne's Park provides one of Dublin's finest green spaces for recreation and leisure.\r\n\r\nThe area is renowned for its excellent sporting facilities, including golf, rugby, GAA, tennis and sailing clubs, along with a wide selection of highly regarded primary and secondary schools. Dublin City Centre, located just 6 kilometres away, is easily accessible via both Dublin Bus services and the nearby DART, making this an ideal location for commuters seeking a balance between city convenience and coastal living.\r\n\r\nWhether you are a first-time buyer, downsizer or someone searching for a character-filled home to transform, No. 6 Brian Boru Street represents a rare opportunity to acquire a piece of Clontarf's architectural heritage in an outstanding location.\r\n\r\nFor further information or to arrange a viewing, contact Hamill Estate Agents today."
      },
